  feature. Alcohol\, cigarettes\, electronic cigarettes\, and illicit drug
 s are prohibited at IU Cinema.        </p></div></div></div></div><div cl
 ass="section bg-none individual-film__intro"><div class="row"><div class=
 "layout"><div class="text"><p><i><strong>Best Wishes to All</strong></i><
 strong>/</strong><i><strong>Mina ni sachi are</strong></i><strong>(Yûta 
 Shimotsu\, Japan\, 2023):</strong> A young woman's visit to her grandpare
 nts' home leads to the discovery of what's brought them happiness\, a rev
 elation that will lead her to question her choices\, sanity\, and reality
  itself. [89 min\; horror\; Japanese with English subtitles]        </p><
 p><i><strong>Gozu</strong></i><strong>(Takashi Miike\, Japan\, 2003):</st
 rong> Acclaimed director Takashi Miike's unhinged Yakuza/horror film cont
 inues to shock and amaze audiences decades after its original release. Mi
 nami is sent to kill his mentor Ozaki (who is in the midst of a nervous b
 reakdown) but soon finds the simple hit quickly morphs into a terrifying 
 and visceral journey into the unexplained and unknown. One of the films i
