SUMMARY:Lilly Library Photography Collection Visit
DTSTART:20261102T170000Z
DTEND:20261102T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260925T105856Z
UID:20261102T170000Z-2430770@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261102T170000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1200,800/32706_20190517_SummerCampusScenics_JB_0078.rev.1
 790344327.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Lectures, talks, seminars, and confe
 rences
DESCRIPTION:Join the Lilly Library's Curator of Photography for this behin
 d-the-scenes look at photographs from their permanent collection. As India
 na University's main library for rare books\, manuscripts\, and special co
 llections participants will learn the role that photography plays througho
 ut the Lilly Library's collections. In addition to viewing a wonderful sel
 ection from throughout photographic history\, we will get to hear about th
 e upcoming exhibition Harnessing Light: Tracing Time Through Photography o
 pening at the Lilly Library early next year.Scott McMahon is Curator of Ph
 otography at the Lilly Library. His primary areas of research involve hist
 oric/antiquarian processes and the production of his own photographic work
 s using wet plate collodion\, gum bichromate\, anthotype\, and cyanotype\,
  as well as camera obscuras and homemade pinhole cameras. Prior to joining
  the Lilly Library team\, Scott was Professor of Art at Columbia College (
 Columbia\, MO) where he taught darkroom and digital photography and course
 s in the history of photography. Scott received his M.F.A. in Photography 
 from Massachusetts College of Art &amp\; Design in Boston\, MA. His work c
 an be seen at scottmcmahonphoto.com (https://scottmcmahonphoto.com/).
GEO:39.167909;-86.518974
LAST-MODIFIED:20260928T161450Z
LOCATION:LILLY LIBRARY
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2430763-lilly-library-photography-co
 llection-visit
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join the Lilly Library's Curator of Phot
 ography for this behind-the-scenes look at photographs from their permanen
 t collection. As Indiana University's main library for rare books\, manusc
 ripts\, and special collections participants will learn the role that phot
 ography plays throughout the Lilly Library's collections. In addition to v
 iewing a wonderful selection from throughout photographic history\, we wil
 l get to hear about the upcoming exhibition <em>Harnessing Light: Tracing 
 Time Through Photography</em> opening at the Lilly Library early next year
 .</p><p style="font-weight: 400\;"><strong>Scott McMahon</strong> is Curat
 or of Photography at the Lilly Library. His primary areas of research invo
 lve historic/antiquarian processes and the production of his own photograp
 hic works using wet plate collodion\, gum bichromate\, anthotype\, and cya
 notype\, as well as camera obscuras and homemade pinhole cameras. <strong>
 </strong>Prior to joining the Lilly Library team\, Scott was Professor of 
 Art at Columbia College (Columbia\, MO) where he taught darkroom and digit
 al photography and courses in the history of photography. Scott received h
 is M.F.A. in Photography from Massachusetts College of Art &amp\; Design i
 n Boston\, MA. His work can be seen at <a href="https://scottmcmahonphoto.
 com/">scottmcmahonphoto.com</a>.</p>
