X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_64
SUMMARY:Gouged: A Conversation with Lindsay Owens on Price Gouging
DTSTART:20261102T170000Z
DTEND:20261102T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20261028T125155Z
UID:20261102T170000Z-2466348@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261102T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:Why do prices go up quickly but come down slowly\, if they com
 e down at all? When does a price increase stop being normal market behavio
 r and become exploitation? The Antitrust and Consumer Protection Law Assoc
 iation invites you to an interview with Lindsay Owens\, author of Gouged\,
  to explore those questions.  The interview will be followed by an audienc
 e Q&amp\;A. Whether you're interested in antitrust\, consumer protection\,
  regulatory policy\, or simply understanding why everything costs more\, t
 his event is a chance to engage directly with one of the leading voices on
  corporate pricing power.
GEO:39.165074;-86.526424
LAST-MODIFIED:20261028T214622Z
LOCATION:Lowell E. Baier Hall - Lecture Room - 125
URL:https://events.iu.edu/lawiub/event/2466348-gouged-a-conversation-with-
 lindsay-owens-on-price
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Why do prices go up quickly but come dow
 n slowly\, if they come down at all? When does a price increase stop being
  normal market behavior and become exploitation? The Antitrust and Consume
 r Protection Law Association invites you to an interview with Lindsay Owen
 s\, author of Gouged\, to explore those questions.<br />  The interview wi
 ll be followed by an audience Q&amp\;A. Whether you're interested in antit
 rust\, consumer protection\, regulatory policy\, or simply understanding w
 hy everything costs more\, this event is a chance to engage directly with 
 one of the leading voices on corporate pricing power.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>Robert Martin<br />\nAntitrust &amp\; Consumer
  Protection Law Assc</p>
