 ies\, into sophisticated\, culturally grounded works infused with clarity
 \, wit\, and nuance. As a Korean American\, Kim explores the localization
  of imported traditions\, incorporating cross-cultural elements that have
  drawn the interest of orchestras and conductors worldwide. Characterized
  by "exuberant\, colorful washes of sound" (<em>San Diego Story</em>)\, h
 is music is at times "explosively virtuosic" (<em>Wall Street Journal</em
 >) yet consistently uplifting and rewarding for both listeners and perfor
