 \, Copland House\, and SCI/ASCAP\, as well as the Barlow Prize and the Is
 ang Yun International Composition Prize. Kim previously taught at San Die
 go State University and Syracuse University. He has also served as artist
 -of-the-year with the Busan Philharmonic Orchestra and composer-in-reside
 nce with the Korean National Symphony Orchestra\, where he launched the C
 omposers' Atelier program to educate and commission emerging composers. A
  Jacobs School alumnus\, his mentors include Unsuk Chin\, Sangjick Jun\, 
 David Dzubay\, Claude Baker\, and Sven-David Sandström. He is represente
 d by Summers Artist Services and published by Bill Holab Music.<br /><br 
