BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 135": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2403547-black-sea-security-lecture-russia-in-europe-and-the-"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_135
SUMMARY:Black Sea Security Lecture: "Russia in Europe and the Middle East:
  Two Theaters\, One Strategy" with Iulia Joja
DTSTART:20261104T192000Z
DTEND:20261104T202000Z
DTSTAMP:20260923T152418Z
UID:20261104T192000Z-2428190@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261104T192000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/182/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,481,558/32310_image.rev.1788281233.png
DESCRIPTION:Russia's convergence with Iran — shared targeting data\, dro
 ne shipments\, sanctions evasion — links the Black Sea to the Strait of 
 Hormuz\, yet NATO still treats these as separate theatres. As Senator Rich
 ard Lugar warned in 1993\, "NATO will either develop a strategy and struct
 ure to go 'out of area' or it will 'go out of business.'" This talk argues
  Russia's challenges demand one integrated transatlantic strategy.  Iulia 
 Joja is a senior fellow at the Middle East Institute\, where she focuses o
 n the intersection between Europe and the Middle East. She is also an adju
 nct professor at Georgetown University and George Washington University\, 
 teaching European security.Cosponsored by The Byrnes Institute (REEI)\, th
 e Jean Monnet Chair\, and the Center for the Study of the Middle East
GEO:39.169199;-86.515674
LAST-MODIFIED:20260923T192418Z
LOCATION:STEPHEN L. &amp\; CONNIE J. FERGUSON INTERNATIONAL CENTER
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2403547-black-sea-security-lecture-r
 ussia-in-europe-and-the-
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Russia's convergence with Iran — share
 d targeting data\, drone shipments\, sanctions evasion — links the Black
  Sea to the Strait of Hormuz\, yet NATO still treats these as separate the
 atres. As Senator Richard Lugar warned in 1993\, "NATO will either develop
  a strategy and structure to go 'out of area' or it will 'go out of busine
 ss.'" This talk argues Russia's challenges demand one integrated transatla
 ntic strategy.</p><p>  Iulia Joja is a senior fellow at the Middle East In
 stitute\, where she focuses on the intersection between Europe and the Mid
 dle East. She is also an adjunct professor at Georgetown University and Ge
 orge Washington University\, teaching European security.</p><p><em>Cospons
 ored by The Byrnes Institute (REEI)\, the Jean Monnet Chair\, and the Cent
 er for the Study of the Middle East</em></p>
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2428190
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/182/width/168/heigh
 t/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,481\,558/32310_image.rev.1788281233.png
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE-CAPTION:<span style="text-align: left\; text-indent: 0px
 \; background-color: #ffffff\; margin: 0px\; font-family: 'Segoe UI'\, 'Se
 goe UI Web (West European)'\, -apple-system\, BlinkMacSystemFont\, Roboto\
