X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Hamilton Lugar School": "https://events.iu.edu/hls/event/2368472-global-competencies-skills-development-series", "IU Kelley School of Business": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2368472-global-competencies-skills-development-series", "IU La Casa Latino Cultural Center": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2368472-global-competencies-skills-development-series"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 135": "https://events.iu.edu/hls/event/2368472-global-competencies-skills-development-series"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_135
SUMMARY:Global Competencies Skills Development Series: Mapping a Refugee C
 amp — Interactive Policy Simulation with Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Win
 stanley
DTSTART:20261105T150000Z
DTEND:20261105T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20260803T132911Z
UID:20261105T150000Z-2368472@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261105T150000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/135/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,2000,2000/31509_GLOBAL_COMPETENCIES_SKILLS_DEVELOPMENT_SE
 RIES.rev.1784660853.png
CATEGORIES:Career development,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences,T
 raining, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:Real Crisis. Real Decisions. Real Tradecraft.  When displaceme
 nt crises hit\, how do international leaders manage logistics\, security\,
  human rights\, and geopolitical pressure in real time?  Skip the standard
  lecture and get your hands on actual diplomatic decision-making. Join the
  Global Competencies Skills Development Series for Mapping a Refugee Camp\
 , an interactive\, fast-paced crisis response simulation led by Ambassador
  Gina Abercrombie-Winstanley—former U.S. Ambassador to Malta\, 30-year F
 oreign Service veteran\, and President of the Middle East Policy Council. 
  Having led emergency war-zone evacuations and served across Baghdad\, Cai
 ro\, and Jeddah\, Ambassador Abercrombie-Winstanley will guide you through
  the complex tradecraft\, resource constraints\, and tactical choices requ
 ired on the front lines of global humanitarian crisis management.  Who Can
  Attend? Open to all: Students (Undergrad &amp\; Grad)\, Faculty\, Staff\,
  and the Public. (Light snacks and drinks provided)  &#160\;  What You'll 
 Get Out of It      Hands-On Tactical Experience: Practice real-world decis
 ion-making under competing geopolitical\, logistical\, and ethical pressur
 es.          Direct Professional Access: Work through crisis scenarios dir
 ectly alongside a senior diplomat who operated across the State Department
 \, Defense Department\, and National Security Council.          Resume-Bui
 lding Tradecraft: Build core skills in crisis navigation\, strategic negot
 iation\, and rapid resource allocation—essential for careers in foreign 
 policy\, intelligence\, NGOs\, and national security.          Active Netw
 orking: Team up with peers\, faculty\, and practitioners across campus ove
 r light refreshments.      Bio: Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Winstanley  Am
 bassador Gina Abercrombie-Winstanley is a 30-year diplomat\, former U.S. A
 mbassador to the Republic of Malta\, and President of the Middle East Poli
 cy Council. Her career spans executive leadership roles across the Departm
 ent of State\, Defense Department\, National Security Council\, and Senate
  Foreign Relations Committee. She has advised the commander of U.S. cyber 
 forces\, expanded international counterterrorism partnerships\, and led th
 e emergency evacuation of thousands of U.S. citizens from a war zone. She 
 is a recipient of the State Department Superior Honor Award for acts of co
 urage during an al-Qaeda attack on the U.S. Consulate in Jeddah.
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
LAST-MODIFIED:20260810T184818Z
LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING
URL:https://events.iu.edu/hls/event/2368472-global-competencies-skills-dev
 elopment-series
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<h4 data-path-to-node="13">  Real Crisis. Rea
 l Decisions. Real Tradecraft.</h4><p data-path-to-node="14">  When displac
 ement crises hit\, how do international leaders manage logistics\, securit
 y\, human rights\, and geopolitical pressure in real time?</p><p data-path
 -to-node="15">  Skip the standard lecture and get your hands on actual dip
 lomatic decision-making. Join the Global Competencies Skills Development S
 eries for Mapping a Refugee Camp\, an interactive\, fast-paced crisis resp
 onse simulation led by Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Winstanley—former U.S
 . Ambassador to Malta\, 30-year Foreign Service veteran\, and President of
  the Middle East Policy Council.</p><p data-path-to-node="16">  Having led
  emergency war-zone evacuations and served across Baghdad\, Cairo\, and Je
 ddah\, Ambassador Abercrombie-Winstanley will guide you through the comple
 x tradecraft\, resource constraints\, and tactical choices required on the
  front lines of global humanitarian crisis management.</p><h4 data-path-to
 -node="17">  Who Can Attend? Open to all: Students (Undergrad &amp\; Grad)
 \, Faculty\, Staff\, and the Public. <i data-path-to-node="18" data-index-
 in-node="74">(Light snacks and drinks provided)</i></h4><h4 data-path-to-n
 ode="19">  &#160\;</h4><h4 data-path-to-node="19">  What You'll Get Out of
  It</h4><ul data-path-to-node="20"><li><p data-path-to-node="20\,0\,0">   
    Hands-On Tactical Experience: Practice real-world decision-making under
  competing geopolitical\, logistical\, and ethical pressures.    </p></li>
 <li><p data-path-to-node="20\,1\,0">      Direct Professional Access: Work
  through crisis scenarios directly alongside a senior diplomat who operate
 d across the State Department\, Defense Department\, and National Security
  Council.    </p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="20\,2\,0">      Resume-Bui
 lding Tradecraft: Build core skills in crisis navigation\, strategic negot
 iation\, and rapid resource allocation—essential for careers in foreign 
 policy\, intelligence\, NGOs\, and national security.    </p></li><li><p d
 ata-path-to-node="20\,3\,0">      Active Networking: Team up with peers\, 
 faculty\, and practitioners across campus over light refreshments.    </p>
 </li></ul><h3 data-path-to-node="22">  Bio: Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Wi
 nstanley</h3><p data-path-to-node="23">  Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Winst
 anley is a 30-year diplomat\, former U.S. Ambassador to the Republic of Ma
 lta\, and President of the Middle East Policy Council. Her career spans ex
 ecutive leadership roles across the Department of State\, Defense Departme
 nt\, National Security Council\, and Senate Foreign Relations Committee. S
 he has advised the commander of U.S. cyber forces\, expanded international
  counterterrorism partnerships\, and led the emergency evacuation of thous
 ands of U.S. citizens from a war zone. She is a recipient of the State Dep
 artment Superior Honor Award for acts of courage during an al-Qaeda attack
  on the U.S. Consulate in Jeddah.</p>
