DESCRIPTION:Art can be anything that inspires us—a painting\, a building
 \, a fashion collection\, a photograph\, a piece of music\, a place\, or e
 ven an everyday object that changes the way we see the world.  In collabor
 ation with the Art Therapy Program at the Eskenazi Museum\, Art That Chang
 ed Me invites attendees to share one image (physical or digital) and one s
 tory about something that has inspired\, challenged\, or shaped who they a
 re.  Through brief 3–5 minute presentations\, participants will celebrat
 e the diverse experiences\, passions\, and creative journeys that make up 
 our community while exploring the powerful connections between creativity\
 , reflection\, and wellbeing.  Participants are encouraged to bring their 
 content ready to go on a flash drive to enable ease of loading in for thei
 r presentations quickly.
