DESCRIPTION:Highlighting a variety of works in the Eskenazi Museum of Art\
 , including the Samuel Levi Jones: An Archeology of Knowledge exhibition\,
  we'll consider sustainability beyond the environment and explore what we 
 value—and hope for —in building a future for generations to come.About
  Your Guide  Blake Nietert is a Marketing\, International\, and Sustainabl
 e Business major with a minor in Art History. With five semesters of exper
 ience leading tours at the Eskenazi Museum of Art\, he is slowly convincin
 g himself that he has seen the artworks move when no one is watching.  Whi
 le especially passionate about European art\, Blake loves exploring and re
 searching art from around the world. He finds that the Eskenazi Museum of 
 Art always offers a new perspective on life when he needs it most. Blake l
 eads Art Investigator Tours\, Teen Gallery Walks\, and a variety of specia
 lty tours\, sharing his enthusiasm for art and creating engaging experienc
 es for museum visitors  &#160\;  Know Before You GoWalk-ins are welcome if
  space is available. Check in with Guest Services on the first floor.&#160
 \;A small handbag may be carried at your side. Backpacks and large bags wi
 ll need to be stored before touring. Learn more aboutmuseum guidelines.If 
 you park in the IMU parking lot\, Guest Services can validate your parking
  voucher for a discount.Read aboutwhere to find us and where to park\,
