SUMMARY:First Thursday Declaration of Independence Lecture
DTSTART:20261105T223000Z
DTEND:20261105T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260914T121646Z
UID:20261105T223000Z-2417193@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261105T223000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,600,600/32759_lilly_nov_first_thurs_lw_square_avatar.rev.
 1790711261.jpg
CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:As part of our yearlong America 250 programming\, IU Associate
  Professor of History Konstantin Dierks will give a talk entitled "Resonan
 ces of the Declaration of Independence in American History."  Is it worth 
 commemorating the Declaration of Independence in 2026? Does the Declaratio
 n still have resonance in our time of terrible crisis? The Declaration exp
 ressed ideals with intensely contested and severely limited meanings in 17
 76. Yet those brittle ideals somehow carried forward through American hist
 ory. Looking closely at the complexities of 1776 can help us ponder how th
 e Declaration might speak to our crisis in 2026.  Before and after the tal
 k\, please feel free to peruse our Declaration of Independence exhibitions
 : The Motives\, The Moment and The Signers.
GEO:39.167909;-86.518974
LAST-MODIFIED:20261008T210845Z
LOCATION:LILLY LIBRARY
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2394856-first-thursday-declaration-o
 f-independence-lecture
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  As part of our yearlong America 250 prog
 ramming\, IU Associate Professor of History Konstantin Dierks will give a 
 talk entitled "Resonances of the Declaration of Independence in American H
 istory."</p><p style="padding-left: 40px\;">  Is it worth commemorating th
 e Declaration of Independence in 2026? Does the Declaration still have res
 onance in our time of terrible crisis? The Declaration expressed ideals wi
 th intensely contested and severely limited meanings in 1776. Yet those br
 ittle ideals somehow carried forward through American history. Looking clo
 sely at the complexities of 1776 can help us ponder how the Declaration mi
 ght speak to our crisis in 2026.</p><p>  Before and after the talk\, pleas
 e feel free to peruse our <em>Declaration of Independence</em> exhibitions
 : <em>The Motives\, The Moment</em> and <em>The Signers</em>.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  <strong>Lilly Library</strong><br />\n  li
 blilly@iu.edu\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2417193
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/heigh
 t/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,600\,600/32759_lilly_nov_first_thurs_lw_squa
 re_avatar.rev.1790711261.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-RSVP:1
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>\n  IU Libraries Lilly Library invites you to a spe
 cial First Thursday talk in conjunction with our Declaration of Independen
 ce exhibitions.\n</p>
