BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 64": "https://events.iu.edu/lawiub/event/2435593-ilj-symposium-evolving-frontiers-in-criminal-law"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_64
SUMMARY:ILJ Symposium: Evolving Frontiers in Criminal Law: Pregnancy\, Fam
 ily\, and Identity
DTSTART:20261106T134500Z
DTEND:20261106T211500Z
DTSTAMP:20260930T083050Z
UID:20261106T134500Z-2435593@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261106T134500Z
DESCRIPTION:The Symposium originated from the book\, Pink Crime: Fighting 
 Against the Criminalization of Motherhood\, Pregnancy\, and Queer Identity
 \, by IU Maurer School of Law Professor Valena Beety\, a founding board me
 mber of the Indiana Innocence Project. Pink Crime focuses on the ways that
  criminal law is strategically used to limit the bodily autonomy of women 
 and queer people\, combined with a discussion of how the system as a whole
  targets the most vulnerable populations while allowing bias\, stigma\, an
 d unreliable evidence to influence prosecution decisions\, especially in s
 ituations where no crime occurred at all.  This Symposium seeks to expand 
 upon Professor Beety's work in Pink Crime by bringing in expert perspectiv
 es to illustrate how existing and developing legal mechanisms strip away b
 asic rights and lay the groundwork for more oppressive measures in the fut
 ure. This area of law is evolving too quickly for large portions of the le
 gal academy to keep up. Therefore\, this Symposium aims to analyze the leg
 al\, social\, and political dimensions of identity criminalization and pro
 vide timely theory\, analysis\, and practical solutions for professionals 
 to draw on as we move forward.  This symposium is offered both in person a
 nd online. Each panel has been approved for one (1) hour of in-person or v
 irtual CLE credit by the Indiana Office of Admissions and Continuing Educa
 tion. Please RSVP at the bottom of this page to attend in person. Zoom reg
 istration is available by panel below. ILJ associates are required to atte
 nd at least two panels. Attendance will be taken.View the full agenda. (ht
 tps://events.iu.edu/live/files/8496-ilj-symposium-agenda-publicpdf)ZOOM WE
 BINAR REGISTRATIONOpening Remarks &amp\; Prosecution of Pregnancy (Panel 1
 ) Register for Zoom (https://iu.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_W_4FzIBRRsaxZQ
 WLx-O5Bw)Criminal Law After Dobbs (Panel 2) Register for Zoom (https://iu.
 zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_50EaYXAiTDOEA5ouDYnhkw)Family Regulation and C
 riminal Law (Panel 3) Register for Zoom (https://iu.zoom.us/webinar/regist
 er/WN_KP47CXL4Rn6GzrdNEjOSpQ)Criminalizing Queer Life and Family (Panel 4)
  Register for Zoom (https://iu.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_tM-sch02TdKdlIl
 NL5URfA)Systemic Failures Along the Path to Wrongful Convictions (Panel 5)
  &amp\; Closing Remarks Register for Zoom (https://iu.zoom.us/webinar/regi
 ster/WN_yocH6mKWQd-hWRjkezuLzA)  We acknowledge IU Research and the Resear
 ch Conference Grant program for its generous funding and support of this s
 ymposium.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261029T154456Z
LOCATION:LOWELL E. BAIER HALL/IU MAURER SCHOOL OF LAW
URL:https://events.iu.edu/lawiub/event/2435593-ilj-symposium-evolving-fron
 tiers-in-criminal-law
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  The Symposium originated from the book\,
  <em>Pink Crime: Fighting Against the Criminalization of Motherhood\, Preg
 nancy\, and Queer Identity</em>\, by IU Maurer School of Law Professor Val
 ena Beety\, a founding board member of the Indiana Innocence Project. <em>
 Pink Crime</em> focuses on the ways that criminal law is strategically use
 d to limit the bodily autonomy of women and queer people\, combined with a
  discussion of how the system as a whole targets the most vulnerable popul
 ations while allowing bias\, stigma\, and unreliable evidence to influence
  prosecution decisions\, especially in situations where no crime occurred 
 at all.</p><p>  This Symposium seeks to expand upon Professor Beety's work
  in <em>Pink Crime</em> by bringing in expert perspectives to illustrate h
 ow existing and developing legal mechanisms strip away basic rights and la
 y the groundwork for more oppressive measures in the future. This area of 
 law is evolving too quickly for large portions of the legal academy to kee
 p up. Therefore\, this Symposium aims to analyze the legal\, social\, and 
 political dimensions of identity criminalization and provide timely theory
 \, analysis\, and practical solutions for professionals to draw on as we m
 ove forward.</p><p>  This symposium is offered both in person and online. 
 Each panel has been approved for one (1) hour of in-person or virtual CLE 
 credit by the Indiana Office of Admissions and Continuing Education. Pleas
 e RSVP at the bottom of this page to attend in person. Zoom registration i
 s available by panel below. <strong><span style="text-decoration: underlin
 e\;">ILJ associates are required to attend at least two panels. Attendance
  will be taken.</span></strong></p><p><strong><a class="file file_8496 lw_
 files_pdf" title="ILJ Symposium Agenda - Public.pdf" href="https://events.
 iu.edu/live/files/8496-ilj-symposium-agenda-publicpdf" target="_blank" rel
 ="noopener">View the full agenda.</a></strong></p><p><span style="text-dec
 oration: underline\;"><strong>ZOOM WEBINAR REGISTRATION</strong></span></p
 ><ul><li>Opening Remarks &amp\; Prosecution of Pregnancy (Panel 1) <a href
 ="https://iu.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_W_4FzIBRRsaxZQWLx-O5Bw">Register 
 for Zoom</a></li><li>Criminal Law After Dobbs (Panel 2) <a href="https://i
 u.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_50EaYXAiTDOEA5ouDYnhkw">Register for Zoom</a
 ></li><li>Family Regulation and Criminal Law (Panel 3) <a href="https://iu
 .zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_KP47CXL4Rn6GzrdNEjOSpQ">Register for Zoom</a>
 </li><li>Criminalizing Queer Life and Family (Panel 4) <a href="https://iu
 .zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_tM-sch02TdKdlIlNL5URfA">Register for Zoom</a>
 </li><li>Systemic Failures Along the Path to Wrongful Convictions (Panel 5
 ) &amp\; Closing Remarks <a href="https://iu.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_y
 ocH6mKWQd-hWRjkezuLzA">Register for Zoom</a></li></ul><p>  We acknowledge 
 IU Research and the Research Conference Grant program for its generous fun
 ding and support of this symposium.</p>
