X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 135": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2443087-aces-horizon-talk-the-soviet-factor-in-chinas"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_135
SUMMARY:ACES Horizon Talk: ""The Soviet Factor in China's Regional Ethnic 
 Autonomy: A Sino-Soviet Comparison of Institutions and Ethnic Elites." by 
 Dr. Jun Kumakura
DTSTART:20261109T170000Z
DTEND:20261109T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20261008T064138Z
UID:20261109T170000Z-2444177@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261109T170000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/176/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1275,1650/32940__Horizon_page-0001.rev.1791399120.jpg
CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:Since the founding of the Chinese Communist Party in the 1920s
 \, the Party advocated the idea of a federal state under the influence of 
 the Soviet Union. In 1949\, however\, shortly before the founding of the P
 eople's Republic of China\, the CCP turned toward a form of state-building
  different from federalism and adopted regional ethnic autonomy. While thi
 s shift is often understood as reflecting China's distinctive approach to 
 state-building\, the Soviet dimension—including Stalin's apparent accept
 ance of the CCP's decision—has received comparatively little attention. 
  Drawing on research developed from his doctoral dissertation\, Professor 
 Jun Kumakura examines the Soviet influence on the CCP's system of regional
  ethnic autonomy and traces the subsequent divergence between Chinese and 
 Soviet policies toward ethnic elites.Date &amp\; Time:  Monday\, November 
 9  12:00 PM – 1:30 PMLocation:  GISB 1060This talk will be held in perso
 n only. Lunch will be provided.  This event is sponsored by:Central Eurasi
 an Studies (CEUS)The Inner Asian and Uralic National Resource Center (IAUN
 RC)The Byrnes Institute (REEI)The East Asian Studies Center (EASC)
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
LAST-MODIFIED:20261008T104138Z
LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2443087-aces-horizon-talk-the-soviet
 -factor-in-chinas
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Since the founding of the Chinese Commun
 ist Party in the 1920s\, the Party advocated the idea of a federal state u
 nder the influence of the Soviet Union. In 1949\, however\, shortly before
  the founding of the People's Republic of China\, the CCP turned toward a 
 form of state-building different from federalism and adopted regional ethn
 ic autonomy. While this shift is often understood as reflecting China's di
 stinctive approach to state-building\, the Soviet dimension—including St
 alin's apparent acceptance of the CCP's decision—has received comparativ
 ely little attention.</p><p>  Drawing on research developed from his docto
 ral dissertation\, Professor Jun Kumakura examines the Soviet influence on
  the CCP's system of regional ethnic autonomy and traces the subsequent di
 vergence between Chinese and Soviet policies toward ethnic elites.</p><p><
 strong>Date &amp\; Time:</strong><br />  Monday\, November 9<br />  12:00 
 PM – 1:30 PM<br /><br /><strong>Location:</strong><br />  GISB 1060</p><
 p><strong>This talk will be held in person only. Lunch will be provided.</
 strong></p><p>  This event is sponsored by:</p><ul><li><em>Central Eurasia
 n Studies (CEUS)</em></li><li><em>The Inner Asian and Uralic National Reso
 urce Center (IAUNRC)</em></li><li><em>The Byrnes Institute (REEI)</em></li
 ><li><em>The East Asian Studies Center (EASC)</em></li></ul>
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2444177
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/176/width/168/heigh
 t/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,1275\,1650/32940__Horizon_page-0001.rev.1791
 399120.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE-CAPTION:Dr. Jun Kumakura (熊倉潤)&#160\;is a professo
 r of law and global politics at Hosei University in Japan.
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>The Association of Central Eurasian Students (ACES)
  warmly invites you to an upcoming Horizon Talk titled "<em>The Soviet Fac
 tor in China's Regional Ethnic Autonomy: A Sino-Soviet Comparison of Insti
 tutions and Ethnic Elites</em>"\, featuring Dr. Jun Kumakura from Hosei Un
 iversity\, Japan.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-SOURCE:IU Hamilton Lugar School
END:VEVENT
