X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_135
SUMMARY:What's happening at the COP31 climate summit?
DTSTART:20261111T170000Z
DTEND:20261111T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260923T152455Z
UID:20261111T170000Z-2428208@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261111T170000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/229/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,512,512/32658_COP31-Turkiye-Dikey-Logo_1.rev.1790082648.p
 ng
DESCRIPTION:This November\, delegates from around the world will gather to
  attend the Conference of the Parties (COP) and take stock of global progr
 ess on addressing climate change and to seek pathways toward greater clima
 te action. The conference is convened under the United Nations Framework C
 onvention on Climate Change (UNFCCC) to measure progress and negotiate the
  best ways to address climate change. Parties decide how to cut greenhouse
  gas emissions and adapt to the impacts of climate change\, on Loss and Da
 mage\, and on the means to help countries green their economies and build 
 resilience to climate change.  Join ERI to hear from members of the IU stu
 dent delegation who are participating in COP31 as observers and researcher
 s. Learn about the stakes of this year's conference as well as insights ga
 thered from attendees at this global event.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260923T192455Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2426389-whats-happening-at-the-cop31
 -climate-summit
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  This November\, delegates from around th
 e world will gather to attend the Conference of the Parties (COP) and take
  stock of global progress on addressing climate change and to seek pathway
 s toward greater climate action. The conference is convened under the Unit
 ed Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC) to measure prog
 ress and negotiate the best ways to address climate change. Parties decide
  how to cut greenhouse gas emissions and adapt to the impacts of climate c
 hange\, on Loss and Damage\, and on the means to help countries green thei
 r economies and build resilience to climate change.</p><p>  Join ERI to he
 ar from members of the IU student delegation who are participating in COP3
 1 as observers and researchers. Learn about the stakes of this year's conf
 erence as well as insights gathered from attendees at this global event.</
 p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  Environmental Resilience Institute<br />\n
   eri@iu.edu\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
