DESCRIPTION:Our Open Studio program invites participants to be creative in
  the museum's art studio\, where art becomes a tool for reflection\, expre
 ssion\, and connection. Guided by a trained art therapist\, the open studi
 o welcomes visitors to engage with materials at their own pace while drawi
 ng inspiration from the surrounding exhibitions. No art experience is need
 ed\; just bring your curiosity and a desire to create\, and we'll handle t
 he rest!  Participants are welcome to utilize supplies located in the stud
 io\, as well as bring their own supplies/projects to work on.  This progra
 m occurs during First Thursday each month. It is open to everyone: student
 s\, staff\, and the public included! The group will meet in the Roehm Fami
 ly Art-making Studio\, located inside the Simpson Center for Education on 
 the 2nd floor of the Eskenazi Museum of Art.
