DESCRIPTION:<br>Do you live\, work or play in Monroe County (or South-Cent
 ral Indiana)? Do you want to live in a community where everyone is able to
  thrive? You’re invited to the 2026 Monroe County Childhood Conditions S
 ummit <span dir="ltr">on November 16</span><sup><span dir="ltr">th</span>
 ! </sup><br><br>This year at MC3 we are looking at opportunities to shape
  what surrounds us\, and we look forward to seeing you in November to buil
 d stronger relationships as individuals and organizations to and impact th
 e conditions affecting kids and families in Monroe County and beyond!<br><
 br>From safe and affordable housing\, to economic security\, to zoning\, t
 o climate resilience to healthcare access and beyond\, these social and st
 ructural determinants impact the capacity of children and their caregivers
  alike\, to develop and thrive. When systems and the people within them ar
 e being stretched\, what opportunities do we have to shape what surrounds 
 us in a way that embeds safety\, stability and nurturance into our communi
 ty?<br><br>Register today: <p dir="ltr"><a href="https://2026mc3.eventbr
 ite.com/" target="_blank">https://2026mc3.eventbrite.<wbr />com/</a></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260923T214924Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Monroe County Democratic Party
END:VEVENT
