SUMMARY:Happy Hour at Upland Brewing Co.
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261117T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261117T170000
DTSTAMP:20261031T052006Z
UID:ej1k8s7qjugc4lsa110rgjjaes@google.com__20261117
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20261022T212650Z
DESCRIPTION:Happy hour at Upland's Bloomington brewpub\, Monday to Friday 
 from 3 to 5 PM.\n\n$4 core beers: Dragonfly IPA\, Champagne Velvet\, Wheat
  Ale and Campside.\n\nFood:\n- Chicharrones with smoked chili seasoning\, 
 Bad Elmer's BBQ and lime ($5)\n- Sliders\, $4 each. Burgers: Classic\, Bad
  Elmer's Fav\, Blue Flame\, Inferno\, Beer Cheese or Sweet Plum. Sandwiche
 s: Local Pulled Pork\, Hoosier Tenderloin\, Turkey & Guac.\n- Mini brownie
  with whipped cream\, mint and Bad Elmer's caramel ($4)\n\nDaily beer spec
 ials ($5 pints\, $15 pitchers): Monday Dragonfly IPA\, Tuesday Champagne V
 elvet and CV Light\, Wednesday Wheat Ale\, Thursday Campside Pale Ale\, Fr
 iday rotating draft. Saturday is 20% off barrel-aged sour drafts\, and Sun
 day brings back the Monday to Thursday specials.\n\nTo go: crowlers of any
  core or specialty beer are $10\, or 3 for $25\, every day. Growlers are $
 2 off the Monday to Thursday specials on Wednesday and Sunday.\n\nSpecials
  from Upland's in-house menu as of October 2026 and may change. Check with
  Upland for current offerings.\n\nListed by BloomingtonOnline.com\, your c
 ommunity directory and local news hub for Bloomington and Monroe County.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261022T212653Z
LOCATION:Upland Brewing Co. Brewpub\, 350 W 11th St\, Bloomington\, IN 474
 04
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-SOURCE:BloomingtonOnline Food & Drink
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 11": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2338233-mccalla-open-gallery-hours"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_11
SUMMARY:McCalla Center Open Gallery Hours
DTSTART:20261117T160000Z
DTEND:20261117T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260716T121602Z
UID:20261103T160000Z-2387762@events.iu.edu__20261117
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/479/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,3200,2400/27084_McCalla_Southeast_Side.rev.1753275924.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art, music, films, and performances,Art and museum exhibitions,
 Community events,Functions, festivals, and celebrations
DESCRIPTION:Outfitting IU Athletics: Hoosier Champions                  Th
 is exhibit showcases objects from IU's championship teams and athletes\, c
 onnecting them to historic achievements in the Big Ten and the national st
 age. The items featured in the exhibit are from the IU Athletics Sports Me
 morabilia Collection and feature photos and videos provided by IU Athletic
 s and Indiana University Archives.                Dates: November 14\, 202
 5 - October 2026          &#160\;                  &#160\;        By Their
  Own Hands: The Black Filmmakers Hall of Fame!          Founded in 1974 by
  the Culture and Ethnic Affairs Guild of the Oakland Museum of California\
 , the Black Filmmakers Hall of Fame began as a film lecture series and awa
 rds ceremony celebrating achievements of Black film industry figures. When
  that organization closed\, they donated their materials to IU. In collabo
 ration with the IU Black Film Center and Archive\, this exhibit features o
 bjects from that collection\, including founding documents\, costumes\, an
 d handprints of inductees to the Hall of Fame.        Dates: September 202
 5 - December 2026          &#160\;                  &#160\;        Capturi
 ng the Campus: T.C. Steele\, Indiana University's First Artist in Residenc
 eCapturing the Campus pays tribute to renowned Hoosier artist T.C. Steele.
  The exhibit honors the century that has passed since his death by showcas
 ing paintings form the artist's residency at IU and other relevant works. 
 The exhibit will bring together Steele's landscapes from the IU Public Art
  and Cultural Heritage Collection and the Indiana State Museum and Histori
 c Sites' collection\, allowing the holdings of these two collections to be
  viewed in one space.        Dates: April 17\, 2026 - April 2026          
 &#160\;        Multipurpose Room          Currently Featuring: The Gift of
  Collecting: Tina Jernigan          Jernigan was a passionate supporter of
  both Indiana University and the arts. She donated artworks to the IU Publ
 ic Art and Cultural Heritage Collection upon her passing in 2024. With fun
 ding provided by Jernigan\, Public Art professionally framed\, hung\, and 
 preserved these pieces for this exhibit in the McCalla Building and for fu
 ture installations on campus.&#160\;        Dates: July 2026-July 2027&#16
 0\;  &#160\;  &#160\;  &#160\;
LAST-MODIFIED:20260904T142940Z
LOCATION:McCalla Center\, 525 E. 9th Street\, Bloomington\, Indiana 47408
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2338233-mccalla-open-gallery-hours
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<table style="border-collapse: collapse\; wid
 th: 97.3422%\;" border="1"><tbody><tr><td style="width: 99.9123%\;" colspa
 n="2"><table style="border-collapse: collapse\; width: 97.3422%\;" border=
 "1"><tbody><tr><td style="width: 99.9123%\;"><p style="text-align: center\
 ;"><strong><em>Outfitting IU Athletics: Hoosier Champions</em></strong></p
 ><p style="text-align: left\;">                  This exhibit showcases ob
 jects from IU's championship teams and athletes\, connecting them to histo
 ric achievements in the Big Ten and the national stage. The items featured
  in the exhibit are from the IU Athletics Sports Memorabilia Collection an
 d feature photos and videos provided by IU Athletics and Indiana Universit
 y Archives.                </p><p style="text-align: center\;"><strong>Dat
 es: November 14\, 2025 - October 2026</strong></p><strong><picture class="
 lw_image lw_image29062  lw_align_left"><source media="(max-width: 500px)" 
 type="image/webp" srcset="https://events.iu.edu/live/image/scale/2x/gid/47
