DESCRIPTION:Join the LGBTQ+ Culture Center for World AIDS Day\, an evening
  of remembrance\, reflection\, and hope featuring keynote speaker Ace Robi
 nson\, M.P.H.\, M.H.L.\, Director of Sexual &amp\; Gender Minority (Queer)
  Wellness at Duke University.&#160\;      A nationally recognized HIV poli
 cy advocate and population health expert\, Ace Robinson has spent more tha
 n two decades advancing health equity and supporting communities dispropor
 tionately impacted by HIV. Throughout his career\, he has held leadership 
 roles with organizations including the National Minority AIDS Council (NMA
 C)\, Gay Men's Health Crisis (GMHC)\, the Desmond Tutu Health Foundation i
 n South Africa\, and the David Geffen School of Medicine at UCLA.&#160\;  
     In his keynote\,"Willing Our Way to End the HIV Epidemic\," Robinson w
 ill explore the progress made in HIV prevention and treatment\, the challe
 nges that remain\, and the collective action needed to build a future free
  from stigma\, discrimination\, and health inequities.&#160\;      Followi
 ng the keynote\, participants will have an opportunity to gather in commun
 ity as we honor those lost to HIV/AIDS\, recognize the resilience of peopl
 e living with HIV\, and recommit ourselves to creating a more just and com
 passionate future.      HIV &amp\; STI Testing (IU Health - Positive Link 
 &amp\; Monroe County Health Department) will be provided.  All Indiana Uni
 versity events\, groups\, activities\, educational\, cultural\, and histor
 ical observances welcome all members of the Indiana University community.
GEO:39.16484;-86.520983
LAST-MODIFIED:20261021T195855Z
LOCATION:BIOLOGY BUILDING
URL:https://events.iu.edu/lgbtq/event/2341890-world-aids-day
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<div><p>    Join the LGBTQ+ Culture Center fo
 r World AIDS Day\, an evening of remembrance\, reflection\, and hope featu
 ring keynote speaker <strong>Ace Robinson\, M.P.H.\, M.H.L.</strong>\, Dir
 ector of Sexual &amp\; Gender Minority (Queer) Wellness at Duke University
 .&#160\;  </p><p>    A nationally recognized HIV policy advocate and popul
 ation health expert\, Ace Robinson has spent more than two decades advanci
 ng health equity and supporting communities disproportionately impacted by
  HIV. Throughout his career\, he has held leadership roles with organizati
 ons including the National Minority AIDS Council (NMAC)\, Gay Men's Health
  Crisis (GMHC)\, the Desmond Tutu Health Foundation in South Africa\, and 
 the David Geffen School of Medicine at UCLA.&#160\;  </p><p>    In his key
 note\,<strong>"Willing Our Way to End the HIV Epidemic\,"</strong> Robinso
 n will explore the progress made in HIV prevention and treatment\, the cha
 llenges that remain\, and the collective action needed to build a future f
 ree from stigma\, discrimination\, and health inequities.&#160\;  </p><p> 
    Following the keynote\, participants will have an opportunity to gather
  in community as we honor those lost to HIV/AIDS\, recognize the resilienc
 e of people living with HIV\, and recommit ourselves to creating a more ju
 st and compassionate future.  </p><p>    HIV &amp\; STI Testing (IU Health
  - Positive Link &amp\; Monroe County Health Department) will be provided.
   </p><p><strong>All Indiana University events\, groups\, activities\, edu
 cational\, cultural\, and historical observances welcome all members of th
 e Indiana University community.</strong></p></div>
