 ormation Session will offer guidance on crafting your application and an o
 pportunity to interact with and pose questions to Miller Program Director 
 Daniel Martinez.</p><p class="p1">  The J. Irwin Miller Master of Architec
 ture program is a three-year in-residence program\, with a two-year advanc
 ed placement track possible for students who hold a B.Arch from a NAAB-acc
 redited institution or regional equivalent. With our twin studios approach
 \, students take visual art course alongside architectural studios to deve
 lop their style of architectural design. The three-year program welcome ap
 plicants from a variety of educational and career backgrounds.</p>
