DESCRIPTION:IU Contemporary Dance students have selected artworks in the e
 xhibition as inspiration for an interpretative dance performance at noon. 
 They will perform original choreography\, inspired by the exhibition.  Bef
 ore the dance performance\, join Ben Levy\, Glaubinger Curator of Works on
  Paper\, for a guided short tour to learn more about some of the photograp
 hs that inspired the dance performance.&#160\; &#160\;Read more about this
  exhibition. (https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/exhibitions/2026-08-29-photogr
 aphic-reflex-marks-deprez.html)  &#160\;Know Before You GoNo need to RSVP 
 for this instance.  Meet us at Featured Exhibitions Gallery on the first f
 loor of the Eskenazi Museum.&#160\;  A small handbag may be carried at you
 r side. Larger bags and backpacks will need to be stored before touring. F
 ree lockers are available.&#160\;We recommend arriving a few minutes early
  to store belongings.Admission and tours are free.Read about where to find
  us\, where to park\, accessibility\, and museum guidelines.When You Arriv
 eFor help finding the gallery\, check in with Guest Services staff at the 
 welcome desk on the first floor.If you park in the IMU parking lot\, Guest
  Services can validate your parking voucher for a discount.Store backpacks
  and large bags before touring. Lockers and coat racks are available on th
 e first floor\, past the welcome desk.Keep space (18") between yourself\, 
 including anything you're carrying\, and the art.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260903T113709Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
