SUMMARY:HIV/STI Testing
DTSTART:20261210T150000Z
DTEND:20261210T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260810T150649Z
UID:20261105T150000Z-2376644@events.iu.edu__20261210
DESCRIPTION:Free HIV Testing &amp\; Safer Sex Supplies at the LGBTQ+ Cultu
 re Center  Taking care of your sexual health is an important part of your 
 overall well-being\, and we're committed to making resources accessible\, 
 welcoming\, and judgment-free.Positive Link (https://iuhealth.org/find-med
 ical-services/positive-link-hiv-services) provides free and confidential H
 IV testing in Room 204 of the LGBTQ+ Culture Center every Thursday from 10
 :00 a.m. to 1:00 p.m. during the academic year. During the summer\, testin
 g is available on the first and third Thursdays of each month.  In additio
 n\, during the academic year\, the Monroe County Health Department offers 
 free chlamydia and gonorrhea testing on the third Thursday of every month\
 , also from 10:00 a.m. to 1:00 p.m. in Room 101.  The LGBTQ+ Culture Cente
 r also offers a variety of free safer sex supplies\, including condoms\, i
 nternal condoms\, dental dams\, lubricants\, and educational materials on 
 proper use. These resources are available to all students\, free of charge
 . You can find them in the kitchenette area near the back entrance of the 
 Center and are welcome to take what you need.  STI Testing &amp\; Safer Se
 x Resources Beyond Campus  Prioritizing your sexual health should be simpl
 e and accessible. In addition to services available at the LGBTQ+ Culture 
 Center\, students can receive testing on campus through the IU Student Hea
 lth Center (https://healthcenter.indiana.edu/medical/sti-testing/index.htm
 l) or visit several local organizations (https://healthcenter.indiana.edu/
 health-answers/sexual-health/sti-testing-resources.html) that offer free o
 r low-cost testing and prevention services.  Many of these providers offer
  confidential care\, safer sex supplies\, and supportive information about
  prevention\, treatment\, and sexual wellness. If you're unsure where to s
 tart\, we're happy to help connect you with resources that fit your needs.
 All Indiana University events\, groups\, activities\, educational\, cultur
 al\, and historical observances welcome all members of the Indiana Univers
 ity community.
GEO:39.168722;-86.525274
LAST-MODIFIED:20261027T152557Z
LOCATION:LGBTQ+ CULTURE CENTER
URL:https://events.iu.edu/lgbtq/event/2376644-hivsti-testing
