ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,2400,2400/30936_IMG_9272_2.rev.1776276360.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Functions, festivals, and celebratio
 ns,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences,Training, non-credit classes
 , and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:Designed for K-12 students and their families\, this event off
 ers a fun and flexible way to spark creativity and connect with each other
 . All ages and experience levels are welcome!  Come and go at your own pac
 e. We recommend planning for at least an hour to explore the gallery and m
 ake art.  Start in the Art Studio inside the Kimberly and John Simpson Cen
 ter for Education on the museum's 2nd floor to pick up your Gallery Challe
 nge. Then head to the galleries to find the artwork we'll use as inspirati
 on for our project! When you're ready\, head back to the studio for our ha
 nds-on art-making activity that everyone will love.  This program takes pl
 ace every Second Sunday of the month\, excluding holidays and museum closu
 res. Each month features new artworks and materials\, so there's always so
 mething fresh to explore and create!  All children must be chaperoned.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260917T122131Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/artmuseum/event/2421169-family-art-lab
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Designed for K-12 students and their fam
 ilies\, this event offers a fun and flexible way to spark creativity and c
 onnect with each other. All ages and experience levels are welcome!</p><p>
   Come and go at your own pace. We recommend planning for at least an hour
  to explore the gallery and make art.</p><p>  Start in the Art Studio insi
 de the Kimberly and John Simpson Center for Education on the museum's 2nd 
 floor to pick up your Gallery Challenge. Then head to the galleries to fin
 d the artwork we'll use as inspiration for our project! When you're ready\
 , head back to the studio for our hands-on art-making activity that everyo
 ne will love.</p><p>  This program takes place every Second Sunday of the 
 month\, excluding holidays and museum closures. Each month features new ar
 tworks and materials\, so there's always something fresh to explore and cr
 eate!</p><p>  All children must be chaperoned.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p><strong>Madelyn Cage</strong><br />\n<em>Youth
  and Family Art Education Manager<br /></em>Sidney and Lois Eskenazi Museu
 m of Art<br />\nIndiana University<br />\n<a href="mailto:cagem@iu.edu">ca
 gem@iu.edu<br />\n812-855-0607</a><br />\n<br />\nMadelyn is on maternity 
 leave until November. If you have a question before then\, you can contact
  ematours@iu.edu</p>
