SUMMARY:Mark O’Connor’s An Appalachian Christmas
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261214T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261214T000000
DTSTAMP:20260730T133151Z
UID:MEC-863f1398173973f4eca54015e39ff8ef@browncounty.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261214T000000
SEQUENCE:1
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncounty.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 06/2-scaled.jpeg
CATEGORIES:Entertainment,Family Friendly,Happening,Holiday,Live Music,Thea
 tre &amp\; Entertainment
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260730
DESCRIPTION:Grammy-winning composer and fiddler Mark O’Connor will bring
  An Appalachian Christmas Featuring Maggie O’Connor to Nashville\, Ind.\
 , this holiday season\, with a stop at the Brown County Music Center on Su
 nday\, December 13\, 2026.\nMark O’Connor’s An Appalachian Christmas a
 lbum (2011) reached the #1 ranking on Billboard’s Bluegrass Album charts
 . Hailed by critics from the Wall Street Journal\, New York Times and Los 
 Angeles Times as a top 10 album of the holiday season\, it has become a pe
 rennial classic Christmas recording. For this concert tour\, Mark O’Conn
 or has created several arrangements of Christmas classics and a wondrous m
 ixture of both instrumental and vocal music in bluegrass and other America
 n music genres. Concertgoers are treated to fresh takes on traditional son
 gs with a few original compositions included. His renditions are playful a
 nd joyous\, but can be strikingly earnest too. Mark O’Connor’s Christm
 as concerts feature himself performing on four instruments\; fiddle\, acou
 stic guitar\, mandolin and mandocello\, with his wife and fellow Grammy- w
 inner Maggie O’Connor on fiddle and vocals. Mark and Maggie have perform
 ed An Appalachian Christmas together as husband and wife for nearly 10 yea
 rs\, and together they’ve captured it all on their most recent album A C
 hristmas Duo. Much of the year they tour behind their latest recording of 
 original Americana songs and classics\, Life After Life. Together on stage
 \, Mark and Maggie have a dynamic energy that bring their individual exper
 tise to holiday themes and classics in the most delightful and musically s
 atisfying way!\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260730
LOCATION:200 Maple Leaf Boulevard\, Nashville\, IN 47448
ORGANIZER;CN="Brown County Music Center":MAILTO:boxoffice@browncountymusic
 center.com
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://browncounty.com/events/mark-oconnors-an-appalachian-christmas/
X-SOURCE:Brown County Events
END:VEVENT
