BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Limestone Post": "https://www.playpensports.com/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:limestone_post
SUMMARY:Toddler Sports Classes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20270116T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20270116T120000
UID:26032478t5J4qxuk6WXbMLKaac-g
DESCRIPTION:Playpen Sports Academy is a wonderful way to introduce your ch
 ild to the world of sport and physical activity in a non-intimidating envi
 ronment with a small group of other toddlers and parents. The Playpen Spor
 ts Academy Curriculum is focused on a number of different goals including 
 teaching children how to move and use their bodies\, sharing with other ch
 ildren\, interact in social settings\, follow directions\, and most import
 antly how to have fun in a physically active environment. At Playpen Sport
 s Academy\, we are focused as much on the individual development of your c
 hild as we are on sport specific skills that we teach. Because while we ex
 pect some of your children to go on to be great athletes\, we expect all o
 f your children to go on to be great people!
URL:https://www.playpensports.com/
X-SOURCE:Limestone Post
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Knobstone Hiking Trail Association Of Indiana Meetup": "https://www.meetup.com/knobstone-hiking-trail-association-of-indiana-meetup/events/plpwxtykccbvb/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_knobstone_hiking_trail_association_of_indiana_meetup
X-SOURCE:Knobstone Hiking Trail Association
UID:event_plpwxtykccbvb@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261031T052049Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270116T091500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270116T153000
SUMMARY:2nd Weekend Work Day Trail Building
DESCRIPTION:Knobstone Hiking Trail Association of Indiana Meetup\nWould yo
 u to spend a day in some beautiful woods with a delightful group of people
  building a connecting section of Indiana’s premier long distance hiking
  trail? Come join us as we continue work on the Tecumseh Trail extension p
 ortion of the KHT in MMSF. We will be building the new trail including cli
 pping green briar.\nPlease bring a lunch and water. We will have large han
 d tools\, but please bring any small tools you have such as clippers or a 
 pruning saw. And a backpack is handy to carry everything in. Instructions 
 will be provided for those who need them. We finish about 3:30.\nMeet at t
 he Hatfield Ridge Road parking lot. The gate is open. Go to the big sign o
 n Rosenbaum/Catholic Cemetry Rd.\nJoin us on our website at http://www.kno
 bstonehikingtrail.org/\, on Facebook at [www.facebook.com/groups/225558611
 7953484](http://www.facebook.com/groups/2255586117953484)\, and Substack [
