CREATED:20081013T165254Z
DESCRIPTION: The Community Bike Project is a Bloomington-based organizatio
 n that focuses on providing bike transportation to the people of the city.
  We focus on teaching bicycle maintenence in order to ensure that bikes on
  the streets stay on the streets. Here is what we do: Community Bike Proje
 ct Front Door\n<br><Br>\n\n\n    * bikes for sale: we sell gently used bik
 es at bargain prices\n<br>\n    * earn-a-bike program: participants can re
 ceive a bicycle after volunteering their time in our shop\n<br>\n    * adv
 ocacy: we support alternative forms of transportation\; we support the reu
 se and recycling of bicycles\n<Br>\n    * workshops & classes: we offer un
 ique bike maintence workshops and classes for children and adults\n<br>\n 
    * open shop: we make our tools available to the public\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051226Z
LOCATION:Community Bike Project
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Let's Go! Bloomington
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_bloomington_in_gov_1rosks8nont4ebaq41tfgg8v7g_group_calendar_google_com
SUMMARY:Bloomington Trivia Championship Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270118T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270118T210000
DTSTAMP:20261031T052101Z
UID:4k26ribnh1786sggrmk9l6f6e8@google.com__20270118
SEQUENCE:1
CREATED:20251208T225842Z
DESCRIPTION:<br><br><h2><b>Bloomington Trivia Championship Series</b></h2>
 <h3><b>Held at the Pavilion in <a href="https://switchyardpark.com/"><u>S
 witchyard Park</u></a></b></h3><h4><b>2026 Trivia Nights<br>7-9 p.m.\; doo
 rs open at 6 p.m.</b></h4><ul><li>Friday\, Jan. 16</li><li>Friday\, March 
 27</li><li>Friday\, May 29</li><li>Friday\, July 17</li><li>Friday\, Sept.
  11</li><li>Friday\, Nov. 6</li></ul><p><a href="https://webtrac.bloomingt
 on.in.gov/webtrac/web/search.html?Primarycode=165001"><u>Registration fee 
 is $160 per team for the entire series. Register for all six trivia nights
  by Jan. 16 and save $32!</u></a></p><p><a href="https://webtrac.bloomingt
 on.in.gov/webtrac/web/search.html?Primarycode=165001"><u>Registration dead
 line is the day of the event.</u></a></p><h4><b>Who will be crowned Bloomi
 ngton’s Trivia Champion?</b></h4><p>The winning team from each night wil
 l automatically qualify for the Championship Night. Cumulative point leade
 rs also have a chance to qualify. At the end of the series\, the top teams
  will compete to be Bloomington’s Trivia Champions!</p><p>Prizes will be
  awarded each night to the top three teams.</p><p>The Cabin Restaurant and
  Lounge will be on-site with food\, soda\, beer\, and wine available for p
 urchase.</p><br><br><a href="https://webtrac.bloomington.in.gov/webtrac/we
 b/search.html?Primarycode=165001">Register Now!</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20251208T230205Z
LOCATION:Switchyard Park\, 1601 S Rogers St\, Bloomington\, IN 47403\, USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Parks and Recreation
END:VEVENT
