DTSTART:20270119T174500Z
DTEND:20270119T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20270119T000000Z
SUMMARY:LATS-L 111: LATINO FILM: AN INTRODUCTION AND OVERVIEW (John Nieto-Phillips)
DESCRIPTION:This course examines U.S. films by and/or about Hispanics and 
 Latinos/as (i.e. Mexican-American/Chicano\, Puerto Rican/Boricus\, and 
 Cuban-American.) Throughout the semester we will explore the complex 
 relationship between the constructions of Latino/a identities\, Latino/a 
 stereo-types\, and the circumstances which Latinos encounter in the U.S. as 
 portrayed in film.
